// and it breaks: THE TIDE GOES OUT, told first (the reef cracks, the water streams down into his holes), and he hauls himself up
// out of the nearest one and fights on the dry reef like a crocodile until he dies. Heavy: he drags himself at a walk and turns
// like a boat. THE LUNGE (a red LOW: jump it, or be up on a ledge) drives him ten tiles along the floor, and if it catches you,
// THE DEATH ROLL takes you toward the water in his hole - three swings or a dodge tear you free, and it lets go on its own. A lunge
